<article class="env-lemma" id="035Z">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/035Z">Lemma <span data-tag="035Z">33.6.7</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $X$, $Y$ be schemes over $k$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If $X$ is geometrically reduced at $x$, and $Y$ reduced, then $X \times _ k Y$ is reduced at every point lying over $x$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $X$ geometrically reduced over $k$ and $Y$ reduced, then $X \times _ k Y$ is reduced. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $X$ and $Y$ are geometrically reduced over $k$, then $X \times _ k Y$ is geometrically reduced. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $k$ is perfect and $X$ and $Y$ are reduced, then $X \times _ k Y$ is reduced. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Add more here. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      To prove (1) combine Lemma <a href="/tag/035W" data-tag="035W">33.6.2</a> with Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/034N" data-tag="034N">10.43.5</a>. To prove (2) combine Lemma <a href="/tag/035X" data-tag="035X">33.6.4</a> with Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/034N" data-tag="034N">10.43.5</a>. To prove (3) note that $(X \times _ k Y)_{\overline{k}} = X_{\overline{k}} \times _{\overline{k}} Y_{\overline{k}}$ and use (2) as well as Lemma <a href="/tag/035X" data-tag="035X">33.6.4</a>. To prove (4) use (3) combined with Lemma <a href="/tag/020I" data-tag="020I">33.6.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>